      "writtenOn": "2023-11-24T09:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting. I had a chat with a couple of the Rust experts over here.\nWe agreed that it doesn\u0027t seem worthwhile - it is potentially a pessimisation (it shrinks to fit, which may require allocation + copy), it is potentially less useful to clients, and it doesn\u0027t bring any obvious benefit and makes the code slightly more complicated and slightly less easy to read.\nIt might make more sense in a constrained no_std environment, but that isn\u0027t where we are.",
      "parentUuid": "624afaf9_e176d005",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 20,
